    "prompt": "Explain why a number not divisible by 2 would also not be divisible by 4.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "It is odd, whereas every multiple of $4$ is even.",
      "worked": "A number not divisible by $2$ is odd. Every multiple of $4$ is also a multiple of $2$, so it is even. Therefore an odd number cannot be divisible by $4$.",
